; The Old Crown Vault, under the Sunspire. Down the stair from the palace terrace into the
; antechamber, where two constructs stand asleep either side of the vault doors. Through them, the
; long hall: plates in the floor either side of a runner of gold, darts in the wall above them, a
; pit at the west end with a ledge along the wall, and past it the end of the hall fallen in, where
; the Hollowed have dug up from underneath. Their tunnel runs down to the warden's room, and the
; lever there works the Crown Door in the middle of the hall's north wall. East, the treasury.
; North, through the Crown Door, the relic gallery: shelves and cases of the old kings' things, the
; empty pedestal where the Sunheart sat, and Kael halfway up a shelf at the east end, where the
; sappers come up through the floor once he's called a truce. Lit by gilded lamps and braziers, and
; a little daylight down the stair.

[map]
id = old-crown-vault
name = The Old Crown Vault
tileset = vault
size = 38 36
dark = yes
ambient = 0.12
music = Underground

[legend]
, = floor
s = floor-shadow
x = floor-cracked
